 "applies_to": "Control Techniques HVAC Drive H300 using its onboard BACnet MS/TP port.",
 "summary": "The HVAC Drive H300 has BACnet MS/TP on board. Its fixed object list covers drive analog and digital I/O, a commandable speed reference and run-forward command, reset, output current, torque, frequency, speed and power, status word and last trip, two PID loops, filter-change timers, an energy meter and ten user-selectable AVs that map any drive parameter.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet MS/TP"
 ],
 "firmware": "V01.05.01.10, V01.05.02.02, V02.00.02.02 (PICS)",
 "default_device_instance": null,
 "access_inferred": false,
 "notes": [
  "Object names are listed as printed, including the #AI_01-style prefix.",
  "AV 28-37 map drive parameters chosen in Pr 29.010-29.019; their access follows the mapped parameter (printed R/W).",
  "Binary I/O 1-3 are bi-directional; each can be an input or an output at a time.",
  "The PICS prints the BV descriptions copied from the BO rows; BV descriptions here follow the object names.",
  "The SI-BACnet IP option module uses a different AV numbering (see that list).",
  "Object instantiation is static; objects cannot be created or deleted."
 ],
